:: Mint Random Topic
<<cleareventpool>>
<<if C.npc["Mint Mocha"].dom gt (C.npc["Mint Mocha"].love / 2)>>
    <<addinlineevent "mintdom1">>
        "Seriously, thanks to you all of my friends find it awkward to be around." Mint looks annoyed. "You're like social napalm, freak." Despite the harsh tone, you spend some time with Mint.
    <</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent "mintdom2">>
        "What part of leave me alone do you not understand? You're getting in the way of my training time." Mint huffs in frustration trying to ignore you. Despite the harsh tone, you spend some time with Mint.
    <</addinlineevent>>
<<else>>
	<<addinlineevent "mintlove1">>
        "I'll admit, there are some... upsides to knowing you." Mint blushes slightly but turns away. "That is to say, you help push me to grow stronger. Don't misunderstand." Despite the nice words, she still speaks in a harsh tone. You spend some time with Mint.
    <</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent "mintlove2">>
        "Just because I respect you doesn't mean I'll go easy on you!" Mint huffs with a slight pink tone in her cheeks. "I'll still train super hard and beat you in the next race!" Despite the nice words, she still speaks in a harsh tone. You spend some time with Mint.
    <</addinlineevent>>
<</if>>
<<runeventpool>>
<br><br>
<<if $outside is 1>>
	<<link [[Next|Horse Academy Entrance]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Passout Academy
<<generate1>><<person1>>
You wake several hours later in the infirmary. The room is quiet, save for the soft rustle of curtains swaying in the breeze. It seems one of the students or faculty members carried you here after you collapsed.
<br> <br>
The nurse notices you've woken and approaches your bedside, a grim expression on <<his>> face.
<br><br>
"You're terribly overexerted," <<he>> says. "I understand your desire to improve, but if you keep pushing yourself like this... your body will eventually give out."
<br><br>
You already feel the effects. Every movement is heavier than before.
<br><br>
<span class="red">You feel weaker than before.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<endevent>><<athletics -10>><<danceskill -10>><<physique -10>><<willpower -10>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Tease
<<if $pcWins is 2>>
	"So I guess the first one wasn't beginner's luck after all." You say.
	<br><br>
	Rowan snorts, tugging you in by the shoulder. "Never said it was luck. Said it was you." <<He>> knocks <<his>> forehead lightly against yours. "Startin' to think I oughta trust my own eye more often." <<glove>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	"You sound more relieved than I feel." You laugh.
	<br><br>
	Rowan lets out a short laugh in response, rubbing the back of <<his>> neck. "Yeah, well. Didn't wanna say it before, but that first loss had me a little rattled too." <<His>> hand finds yours. "Glad we got that out of our system." <<glove>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><<set C.npc.Rowan.dom -= 5>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><</link>>

:: Rowan Gloat
<<if $pcWins is 2>>
	You let <<him>> have <<his>> moment, and Rowan takes full advantage of it, throwing an arm around your shoulders and steering you toward the crowd.
	<br><br>
	"Y'all seein' this? Two in a row." <<He>> says it loud enough for anyone nearby to hear, chest puffed out.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances down at you, grin softening. "Knew that first win wasn't a one-time thing. Proud of you." <<glove>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	You let <<him>> have <<his>> moment, and Rowan doesn't waste it, turning toward the crowd with your hand still caught in <<his>>.
	<br><br>
	"Y'all remember that loss last time? Yeah. Don't matter no more." <<He>> grins, unable to help <<himself>>.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> looks back down at you, voice quieter now, just for you. "Real proud of how you bounced back from that. Wanted you to know it." <<glove>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><<set C.npc.Rowan.dom -= 5>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><</link>>

:: Rowan Comfort
<<if $pcWins is 1>>
	"I know. I just wanted to keep the streak going." You say.
	<br><br>
	Rowan glances at you sideways, something soft in <<his>> expression.
	<br><br>
	"Yeah, I figured." <<He>> nudges your shoulder with <<his>>. "But there ain't no streak worth chasin' if it means you beatin' yourself up like this." <<glove>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> keeps walking alongside you, closer than <<he>> needs to.
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	"You really believe that?" You ask.
	<br><br>
	Rowan stops walking for a second, turning to face you fully.
	<br><br>
	"Every word of it." <<He>> reaches out, tilting your chin up so you're looking at <<him>>. "Two losses don't erase what I saw in you the day I picked you out. That ain't goin' nowhere." <<glove>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> doesn't let go right away.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><</link>>

:: Rowan Quiet
You don't say anything.
<br><br>
Rowan doesn't push it. <<He>> walks the rest of the way in silence, and if <<he>>'s worried, <<he>> keeps it tucked somewhere you can't see it.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Comply
You don't argue. There doesn't seem to be much point.
<br><br>
<<He>> watches you for a second, like <<he>> half expected pushback and is mildly thrown by not getting it. Then <<he>> nods once, satisfied, and starts walking. <<gdom>><<glove>>
<br><br>
You follow. Of course, you follow.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><<set C.npc.Rowan.dom += 5>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 3>><</link>>

:: Rowan Push Back
"And if I say no?"
<br><br>
The words are out before you can think better of them.
<br><br>
Rowan stops mid-stride. Turns. For a moment <<he>> just looks at you, something unreadable flickering behind <<his>> eyes.
<br><br>
"You can say no." <<His>> voice is level, almost gentle, which is somehow worse than if <<he>>'d snapped. "Door's right there."
<br><br>
<<He>> tilts <<his>> head toward the exit. Doesn't move otherwise. Just waits, letting the silence stretch, letting you sit with the fact that <<he>> means it.<<gdom>><<llove>>
<br><br>
"But you and I both know you're not gonna walk." <<His>> mouth twitches, not quite a smile. "So let's quit pretendin' and get movin'."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><<set C.npc.Rowan.dom += 5>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love -= 3>><</link>>

:: Rowan Reassure
"We'll figure it out," you say.
<br><br>
Rowan glances at you, surprised for a second, then his shoulders ease, just slightly.
<br><br>
"Yeah." He huffs something close to a laugh. "Yeah, I believe you."
<br><br>
He doesn't say anything else, but he stays a little closer to you on the walk back than he usually does.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><</link>>

:: Rowan Ask Farm
"What happens if we don't make it?"
<br><br>
Rowan's smile falters, just for a second, before he catches it.
<br><br>
"Then I figure somethin' else out." He says it lightly, as it costs him nothing to say, though you can tell it does. "Won't be the first time life's thrown me a curveball."
<br><br>
He bumps your shoulder with his.
<br><br>
"But we're not there yet. So let's not borrow trouble before it's due."<<stress 4>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<set $horseacademycountdown to 7>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Post Race Final
<<npc Rowan>><<person1>>
<<if $raceresult is "win">>
	<<if C.npc.Rowan.love gt 60>>
		Rowan is already moving when you come off the track.<<ldom>><<gglove>>
		<br><br>
		<<He>> catches you at a near-run, arms around you, laughing, properly laughing for the first time in what feels like months, and <<he>> spins you once before <<he>> seems to remember the two of you are in public.
		<br><br>
		When <<he>> sets you down, <<he>>'s grinning so wide it looks like it might hurt.
		<br><br>
		"I knew it." <<He>> cups your face and leans <<his>> forehead against yours. "I knew it. From the very first session, I knew you had it in you."
		<br><br>
		A beat of quiet inside all that noise. <<His>> thumbs brush your cheeks.
		<br><br>
		"The farm's safe," <<he>> breathes. "We're okay."
		<br><br>
		<<His>> eyes are a little bright. You're probably not going to mention that either.
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		You find Rowan at the edge of the track.<<ldom>><<gglove>>
		<br><br>
		<<He>>'s not whooping. <<He>>'s not jumping. <<He>>'s just standing there with <<his>> hat in <<his>> hands, staring at you, like <<he>>'s making sure you're real.<br><br>
		"You did it," <<he>> says.
		<br><br>
		Simple. Quiet. Not even aimed at you particularly. Like <<he>> just needed to hear someone say it out loud.
		<br><br>
		Then <<he>> crosses to you in a few quick strides and grabs you by the back of the head, pressing <<his>> forehead firmly against yours.
		<br><br>
		"You stubborn, hardworking thing—" <<he>> exhales sharply through <<his>> nose. "You did it."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> steps back. Clears <<his>> throat. Puts <<his>> hat back on.
		<br><br>
		"...Good race," <<he>> says, with great dignity.
		<br><br>
		But <<his>> hands are shaking slightly. You both notice. Neither of you mentions it.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Post Race Final 2]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.dom -= 5>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 10>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if C.npc.Rowan.love gt 60>>
		Rowan comes to you.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> always comes to you. That hasn't changed. But when <<he>> reaches you this time <<he>> just stops, a few feet away, and <<his>> face is open in a way you've never quite seen before. All the warmth <<he>>'s always carried right at the surface, and underneath it, something raw and trying very hard not to break.
		<br><br>
		"Hey," <<he>> says.
		<br><br>
		<<His>> voice doesn't sound like <<him>>self.
		<br><br>
		"Rowan, I—"
		<br><br>
		"Don't." <<He>> shakes <<his>> head slowly. "Don't you dare apologise to me. Not for this. Not ever for this."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Comfort <<Him>>|Rowan End Comfort]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Stay Quiet|Rowan End Quiet]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		Rowan is at the track's edge when you come off.<br>
		<br>
		<<He>> looks at you. Just looks, with something in <<his>> face <<he>>'s clearly fighting very hard to keep still.
		<br><br>
		A long moment passes. Long enough that the crowd noise around you starts to feel very far away.
		<br><br>
		Then <<he>> nods once, tightly, like <<he>>'s accepting something <<he>> had hoped, against every shred of sense, wouldn't come.
		<br><br>
		"...Alright." The word comes out flat. Quiet. Like it cost <<him>> something just to get it out.<<npcincr "Rowan" dom 5>>
		<br><br>
		<<He>> doesn't say anything else. <<He>> doesn't reach for you, doesn't smack your shoulder the way <<he>> used to, doesn't do any of the things you've come to expect from <<him>>.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> just turns, and you watch <<him>> walk away across the empty stretch of grass with <<his>> hands buried in <<his>> pockets, shoulders straight, carrying something heavy in a way that won't let anyone see how heavy it is.<<stress 10>> <<ggstress>>
		<br><br>
		You stand there a long time after <<he>>'s gone, watching the spot where <<he>> disappeared, like staring hard enough might bring <<him>> back.
		<br><br>
		It doesn't.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Post Race Final 2]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Post Race Final 2
<<if $raceresult is "win">>
	<<if C.npc.Rowan.love gt 60>>
		Later, once the noise of the day has finally settled, Rowan finds you again, quieter this time, no crowd left to perform for.
		<br><br>
		"Means somethin', you know." <<He>> rubs the back of <<his>> neck, looking almost bashful for once. "Mint Mocha's mine now. Gonna buy her out properly, give her a real shot at somethin' better than just bein' some prize trophy."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> looks at you for a long moment after that, like <<he>>'s deciding something.
		<br><br>
		Then <<he>> steps in close, cups the side of your face with one hand, and presses a slow, bittersweet kiss to your forehead, equal parts relief and something deeper, something that's been building since long before today.
		<br><br>
		"Thank you," <<he>> murmurs against your skin. "For every single morning you showed up. For believin' in this, in me, when you didn't have to."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> finally pulls back, and the smile <<he>> gives you is soft enough to ache.
		<br><br>
		"Reckon we earned a slower mornin' or two, after this."
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		The news about Mint Mocha catches up with you both later that day.
		<br><br>
		Rowan doesn't gloat. <<He>> doesn't say much of anything, actually. <<He>> just goes quiet for a moment, processing the fact that <<his>> rival, the one who's been needling at you both since race one, is now <<his>> to buy outright.
		<br><br>
		"...Gonna treat that horse right," <<he>> finally mutters, mostly to <<himself>>. "Even if she's been a pain in my backside since day one."
		<br><br>
		It's about as close to sentimental as <<he>>'s likely to get about it.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Post Race End]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if C.npc.Rowan.love gt 60>>
		In the days that follow, you learn what's happening to Mint Mocha: sold off, already being advertised under a new owner's banner as a proven winner.
		<br><br>
		Rowan goes quiet when you tell him. <<He>> looks out toward the fields for a long moment, the ones that won't be <<his>> much longer either.
		<br><br>
		"Guess we're both losin' somethin' today," <<he>> says, voice rough.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> turns to you then, and there's nothing guarded left in <<his>> expression, just tired, open honesty.
		<br><br>
		"I don't regret a second of this. Not one." <<He>> reaches up and brushes a strand of hair back from your face, slow and careful, like <<he>>'s trying to memorise the moment. "Wherever I end up, that part doesn't change."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> leans in and presses a slow, lingering kiss to your forehead, the kind that lasts a beat longer than it needs to, like <<he>>'s trying to put everything <<he>> can't say into it instead.
		<br><br>
		When <<he>> finally pulls back, <<his>> eyes are a little too bright.
		<br><br>
		"Thank you," <<he>> murmurs. "For every single morning you showed up."
	<<else>>
		Word travels fast.
		<br><br>
		By the time you find Rowan again, <<he>>'s already heard about Mint Mocha: sold, the new owner already advertising her as a proven winner to recoup the cost twice over.
		<br><br>
		Rowan doesn't say much about it. Doesn't say much about anything, really, in the days that follow. <<He>>'s civil. <<He>>'s practical. <<He>> packs up the farm with the efficiency of a man who's already made his peace with something <<he>> never wanted to make peace with, folding a lifetime into boxes like it's just another chore on the list.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> doesn't blame you. <<He>> never says that <<he>> blames you.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> just doesn't quite look at you the same way anymore, either. There's a distance in <<his>> eyes now that wasn't there before, like <<he>>'s already halfway gone before <<his>> boots have even left the porch.
		<br><br>
		On the last morning, you find <<him>> standing at the fence line, looking out over fields that won't be <<his>> by sundown.
		<br><br>
		"Used to wake up before the sun just to watch the mist come off this grass," <<he>> says, not turning around. "Don't reckon I'll get a view like that again."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> doesn't wait for you to answer. <<He>> just picks up <<his>> bag, and walks toward whatever comes next without you in it.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Post Race End]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Post Race End
<<if $raceresult is "win">>
	<<if C.npc.Rowan.love gt 60>>
		"<<print $playerhorsetitle>>, my lucky star."
		<br><br>
		Rowan laughs under <<his>> breath as <<he>> wraps an arm around your shoulders, still riding the high of the win.
		<br><br>
		"Or should I say..."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> leans in closer, a smug grin tugging at the corner of <<his>> lips.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> murmurs your real name beside one of your horse ears.
		<br><br>
		"There you are."
		<br><br>
		The way <<he>> says it makes your heart skip.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Rowan Epilogue]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">The academy is now closing. Collect your belongings before the entrance is closed for good tomorrow.</span>
		<br><br>
		<span class="gold">You can now visit Rowan's farm starting tomorrow.</span>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Horse Academy Entrance]]>><<set $academycloser to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<span class="red">Rowan is moving out of the farmlands. You likely won't see <<him>> again.
	<br><br>
	Mint Mocha is being sold off to another town. You likely won't see her again either.
	<br><br>
	The academy is now closing. Collect your belongings before the entrance is closed for good tomorrow.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Horse Academy Entrance]]>><<set $academycloser to 1>><<set $rowangone to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Rowan End Comfort
You close the distance between you and wrap your arms around <<him>>.
<br><br>
<<He>>'s still for a half second, surprised, maybe, or just needing a moment to accept it, and then <<his>> arms come around you and <<he>> holds on, steady and tight, face bowed toward your shoulder like <<he>>'s trying to hide there.
<br><br>
<<He>> doesn't cry. But <<his>> breathing is slow and deliberate, the kind of breathing that takes real effort, like someone concentrating on staying upright when every part of them wants to give out.
<br><br>
"We gave it everything," you say quietly, your voice cracking despite yourself.
<br><br>
"Yeah." <<His>> voice is low. Rough. Barely holding together. "Yeah, we did."
<br><br>
<<He>> presses <<his>> face into your hair for a long moment, and you feel <<him>> shudder once, just once, like something finally cracked loose that <<he>>'d been holding shut for a long, long time.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Post Race Final 2]]>><</link>>

:: Rowan End Quiet
You stand there next to each other and watch the other racer accept the trophy, the cheers feeling like they're coming from somewhere very far away.
<br><br>
Rowan's hand finds yours at some point. You're not sure when. <<His>> grip is tighter than it needs to be, like <<he>>'s holding on for both of you. <<His>> thumb moves once, slowly, across your knuckles. Then <<he>> drops it and clears <<his>> throat, blinking hard at nothing in particular.
<br><br>
"Guess that's that, then," <<he>> says quietly. <<His>> voice doesn't quite make it to the end of the sentence steady.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Post Race Final 2]]>><</link>>

:: Rowan Epilogue
"Ain't gonna lie, darlin'," <<he>> chuckles. "Thought I was fixin' to have a heart attack watchin' that final stretch."
<br><br>
<<He>> shakes <<his>> head, still grinning.
<br><br>
"But you went and proved me right."
<br><br>
Rowan gives your shoulder a squeeze.
<br><br>
"Knew you had it in ya from the start. World's finally catchin' up to what I've been sayin' all along."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at you for a moment, pride softening <<his>> usual smug expression.
<br><br>
"Damn. Look at you."
<br><br>
"My champion."
<br><br>
<<He>> goes quiet for a second, something more vulnerable working its way past the easy grin.
<br><br>
"I don't know what comes next for either of us. But I know I don't want to find out without you in it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> you feel the same|Claim Rowan]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> you'd rather stay friends|Platonic Rowan]]>><</link>>

:: Claim Rowan
"I feel the same way."
<br><br>
The words come out steadier than you expected, like they'd been waiting a long time for permission.
<br><br>
Rowan goes still.
<br><br>
Not the easy, lazy stillness you've come to know from <<him>>; something deeper than that. Something that looks, for just a second, like a <<man>> who's been bracing for disappointment for so long <<he>> doesn't quite know what to do when it doesn't come.
<br><br>
"...Yeah?" <<His>> voice cracks, just barely, around the word.
<br><br>
You nod.
<br><br>
That's all it takes.
<br><br>
<<He>> exhales like something in his chest has finally let go, and then <<he>>'s reaching for you, both hands framing your face like <<he>>'s afraid you'll disappear if <<he>> isn't careful. <<His>> forehead drops to yours, and this time there's no humour in it, no teasing, none of the easy deflection <<he>> usually hides behind.
<br><br>
Just <<him>>. Just the truth of it, finally said out loud.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Claim Rowan 2]]>><</link>>

:: Claim Rowan 2
"You have any idea," <<he>> murmurs, voice rough, "how long I been tellin' myself this was just gratitude? That I was just proud of my racer, nothin' more?"
<br><br>
<<His>> thumb brushes along your cheekbone, slow, like <<he>>'s memorizing the shape of this moment.
<br><br>
"Lyin' to myself the whole damn time."
<br><br>
<<He>> tips your chin up gently and presses a kiss to your forehead, lingering there in a way that says everything <<his>> drawl usually dances around. When <<he>> finally pulls back, <<his>> eyes are bright, and the smile <<he>>'s wearing is helpless, unguarded, nothing like the smug grin you first met.<<npcincr "Rowan" love 10>>
<br><br>
"Guess that makes it official, then." <<His>> hand finds yours, fingers lacing through without hesitation, like they were always going to end up there. "You're stuck with me now, <<girl>>. Hope you're ready for that."
<br><br>
<<He>> laughs, soft and a little disbelieving, like the win and the confession together are almost too much to hold at once.
<br><br>
"Been a hell of a season."
<br><br>
<<set $rowanromance to 1>>
<<if $loveInterest.primary is "None">>
	<<set $loveInterest.primary to "Rowan">>
	<span class = "gold">Rowan is now your love interest! You feel like you're in for a wild ride.</span>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<span class = "gold">Rowan can now be claimed as your love interest! You feel like you're in for a wild ride. <br>You can change your love interest in the "Attitudes" menu.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<span class="red">The academy is now closing. Collect your belongings before the entrance is closed for good tomorrow.</span>
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You can now visit Rowan's farm starting tomorrow.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy Entrance]]>><<set $academycloser to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Platonic Rowan
"You'll always have me," you say. "Just not like that."
<br><br>
For a second, something flickers across Rowan's face, too quick to name, gone before you can be sure it was there at all. Then he huffs out a short laugh, and it's easy, genuine, no strain behind it.
<br><br>
"Yeah. Figured that might be the answer." <<He>> rubs the back of <<his>> neck, but <<he>>'s still smiling. "Honestly? Wasn't sure how to ask without makin' things weird."
<br><br>
<<He>> bumps your shoulder with <<his>>, the same easy gesture <<he>>'s given you all season.
<br><br>
"Don't change much, anyway. You're still my <<girl>>." A beat. "Figure of speech. You know what I mean."<<npcincr "Rowan" love 5>>
<br><br>
<<He>> looks almost relieved that you didn't make it complicated, like the friendship was never something <<he>> wanted to risk losing over a maybe.
<br><br>
"C'mon. Let's go tell that ridiculous horse she's got a new home."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy Entrance]]>><<set $rowanconfessed to 1>><<set $academycloser to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>

