<br><br>
Her whole posture shifts, exhaustion forgotten in favor of pure competitive instinct. "You're on. Don't cry when you lose."
<br><br>
The two of you commence an impromptu race, free from the usual racing pressure.
<br><br>
She doesn't beat you by much, but she beats you, and the grin she wears afterward is the most unguarded you've seen her look in weeks, chest heaving, sweat-damp hair stuck to her forehead.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" love 4>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Track Side by Side - Rest
"You've been out here long enough. Go rest."
<br><br>
"Don't tell me what to—" She stops, catches the actual concern under the comment, and the fight drains out of her voice. "...Fine. Five more minutes." She doesn't move for at least ten, but she doesn't argue further either, glancing your way more than once like she's checking you're still there.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" love 3>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mint Bad Day - Push
"You look like someone stole your podium spot. What's wrong?" You ask.
<br><br>
"Nothing's— ugh." She exhales sharply, the irritation draining into something more tired. "Career stuff. Doesn't matter. Peasants wouldn't get it." She says it without much bite, more resigned than defensive, finally setting the phone face-down beside her.
<br><br>
She doesn't elaborate further, but she doesn't tell you to leave either.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" love 3>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mint Bad Day - Space
You decide not to press, sitting down a respectful distance away instead, saying nothing.
<br><br>
She glances over, visibly surprised you didn't ask. After a while, the tension in her shoulders eases, just slightly. "...You're not gonna interrogate me?"
<br><br>
"Nope."
<br><br>
"Huh." She seems to actually relax at that, the silence between you turning almost comfortable by the time she finally gets up to leave.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" love 2>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Caught Staring - Call Out
"See something you like?" You tease.
<br><br>
"Wh— absolutely not!" Her voice cracks slightly on the denial, face flooding with color. "I was checkin' your form! For race purposes! Strictly professional!"
<br><br>
"Sure."
<br><br>
"It was!" She insists, considerably less convincing with every repetition, refusing to look at you again for the rest of practice out of sheer principle.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" love 3>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Caught Staring - Pretend
You let it go without comment, pretending you didn't notice at all.
<br><br>
She seems almost thrown by the lack of reaction, recovering her composure a beat slower than usual. She doesn't bring it up again, but she spends the rest of practice a little too aware of where you are on the track.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mint Walks You Back - Let Him
"Sure. Bad optics."
<br><br>
You don't push it further, and she doesn't offer anything more either, the two of you walking the rest of the way in a silence that's far more comfortable than either of you would admit out loud. At your door, she lingers a beat too long before finally turning to go.
<br><br>
"...G'night," she mutters, already walking away before you can answer, like staying to hear a response would be admitting too much.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" love 4>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Mint Walks You Back - Call Out
"You could just say you wanted to walk with me."
<br><br>
"I could, but I won't, because that's not what's happening." Her ears go red despite the denial, pace picking up slightly. "Don't overanalyze it."
<br><br>
She doesn't slow back down until you're nearly at your door, at which point she seems to remember she was supposed to be unbothered the whole time.<<lsuperiority>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Horse Academy]]>><<npcincr "Mint Mocha" dom -2>><<endevent>><</link>>

